## 4. Calibration Architecture — Zero Compromise

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Calibration quality determines the scientific validity of all outputs. This is non-negotiable and warrants its own dedicated phase.

### 4.1 Calibration Layers (must be performed in order)

```
Layer 1: Lens Intrinsic Calibration
  └── Remove distortion introduced by the physical lens

Layer 2: World Calibration
  └── Map from corrected pixel space to real-world units (m / cm)

Layer 3: Multi-Camera Extrinsic Calibration
  └── Determine spatial relationship between cameras (stereo/multi)
  
Layer 4: Reference Frame Definition
  └── Define world origin, X/Y/Z axes in physical space
```

### 4.2 Lens Distortion Model: Brown-Conrady

```
The full Brown-Conrady model (as used by OpenCV):
  x'' = x'(1 + k1r² + k2r⁴ + k3r⁶) / (1 + k4r² + k5r⁴ + k6r⁶)
       + 2p1x'y' + p2(r² + 2x'²) + s1r² + s2r⁴
  y'' = y'(1 + k1r² + k2r⁴ + k3r⁶) / (1 + k4r² + k5r⁴ + k6r⁶)
       + p1(r² + 2y'²) + 2p2x'y' + s3r² + s4r⁴
```

| Coefficient | Type | Description |
|-------------|------|-------------|
| k1, k2, k3 | Radial | Primary barrel/pincushion distortion |
| k4, k5, k6 | Radial | Rational model (fisheye cameras) |
| p1, p2 | Tangential | Off-center lens (decentering) |
| s1–s4 | Thin prism | Sensor tilt correction |

### 4.3 Calibration Methods Supported

| Method | Pattern Used | Accuracy | When to Use |
|--------|-------------|----------|-------------|
| **ChArUco Board** (recommended) | ArUco + Chessboard hybrid | Highest | Lab setup, first-time calibration |
| **Chessboard (OpenCV)** | Classic checkerboard | High | Standard lab cameras |
| **Known-length stick** | User-drawn line | Good | Post-hoc world scale only |
| **Known world points** | 2+ marked GPS/physical points | Good | Outdoor / field use |
| **Built-in Lens Profile** | Library (GoPro, iPhone, etc.) | Moderate | Quick setup |

### 4.4 Calibration Quality Reporting
After any calibration step, the app must show:
- **RMS Re-projection Error** (target: < 0.5 pixels for lab, < 1.5 pixels for field)
- **Visual re-projection overlay** — draw detected pattern points vs re-projected points on video
- **Distortion map visualization** — heat-map showing per-pixel distortion magnitude
- **Explicit user confirmation** required before calibration is "accepted"

