## 7. CDSCO / IEC 62304 Compliance & Living Documentation

### 7.1 Key Principle: Documentation Lives With Code

> [!IMPORTANT]
> No PR is mergeable if it adds or changes a requirement-related feature without also updating the corresponding documentation files. This is enforced by CI.

Every PR that touches:
- `Calibration/` → must update `SOFTWARE_REQUIREMENTS.md` (new REQ-CAL-xxx), `TRACEABILITY_MATRIX.md`, `CALIBRATION_GUIDE.md`
- `Tracking/` → must update `TRACEABILITY_MATRIX.md`
- Any `ITrackingEngine` → must add a determinism golden baseline test
- Any physics formula → must add a numerical accuracy test with documented expected tolerance

### 7.2 Required Documents Per Phase

| Phase | Documents Updated |
|-------|------------------|
| 1 | SRS (REQ-TRK), SDD (video/canvas arch), Risk (RSK-001, 003) |
| 2 | SRS (REQ-CAL), SDD (calibration arch), Risk (RSK-002), `CALIBRATION_GUIDE.md` |
| 3 | SRS (REQ-TRK tracking), Traceability (all tracking reqs), Bench test reports |
| 4 | SRS (REQ-PHY, REQ-GAIT), Risk (RSK-004 gait computed incorrectly) |
| 5 | SRS (REQ-CAM), SDD (multi-camera/capture arch), Risk (RSK-005 sync error) |
| 6 | SRS (REQ-EXP), Traceability (export reqs), Verification results |
| 7 | SRS (REQ-FLT) |
| 8 | All docs finalized, archival copy in `docs/releases/v1.0.0/` |

### 7.3 Risk Register (Expanded)

| Risk ID | Hazard | Mitigation |
|---------|--------|------------|
| RSK-001 | Non-deterministic tracking | Byte-exact CI determinism tests |
| RSK-002 | Incorrect calibration scale | RMS gate + mandatory explicit user approval |
| RSK-003 | Frame dropping distorting timing | Frame-exact FFmpeg extraction, hardware timestamps |
| RSK-004 | Incorrect gait parameters treated as clinical fact | Prominent "analysis tool, not diagnostic" watermark on reports |
| RSK-005 | Multi-camera sync error causing 3D errors | HW trigger preferred; SW sync lag measured and reported |
| RSK-006 | Lens distortion not corrected before world calibration | UI enforces order: must complete lens correction before world cal |

